{"type":"result","subtype":"success","is_error":false,"duration_ms":397217,"duration_api_ms":480236,"num_turns":33,"result":"","stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"669f56a9-4807-4ffe-a94b-e8add7b2697d","total_cost_usd":1.9029610000000008,"usage":{"input_tokens":4091,"cache_creation_input_tokens":87877,"cache_read_input_tokens":1332431,"output_tokens":14077,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":87877,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-opus-4-6":{"inputTokens":4091,"outputTokens":14077,"cacheReadInputTokens":1332431,"cacheCreationInputTokens":87877,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":1.58782675,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":64000},"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001":{"inputTokens":243,"outputTokens":14073,"cacheReadInputTokens":1213650,"cacheCreationInputTokens":98529,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.31513425,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":32000}},"permission_denials":[],"structured_output":{"summary":"Reviewed the molt mineral budget implementation across shrimp.rs (core mechanics), biology.rs (types/params), neocaridina_davidi.toml (species data), presets.rs (loading), invariants.rs (enforcement), and the test suite (molt_mineral_budget.rs, e2e tests). The implementation is well-structured with properly parameterized thresholds, comprehensive diagnostic event reporting, and tests covering all acceptance criteria. Found one correctness gap in the critical_gh_deficit guard logic, and one gap in cold-temperature molt stress tracking.","amendments":[{"body":"In `shrimp.rs` line 554, the `critical_gh_deficit` check `(gh_d / params.gh_min_d.max(0.01)) < params.critical_molt_gh_ratio` does not guard against `gh_min_d = 0.0` the same way `molt_mineral_modifier` does. When a user sets `gh_min_d = 0.0` (semantically 'no GH minimum'), the `.max(0.01)` guard converts it to 0.01, causing any GH below `0.01 * critical_molt_gh_ratio = 0.003` to falsely trigger a critical deficit override. The fix is to add a check: `let critical_gh_deficit = params.gh_min_d > 0.0 && (gh_d / params.gh_min_d.max(0.01)) < params.critical_molt_gh_ratio;`. The existing test `test_zero_ca_and_mg_min_parameters_use_defensive_guards` (line 411) does not check `last_molt_success` and misses this edge case — it should assert that molt succeeds when all minimums are disabled.","rationale":"Inconsistent edge-case handling between `molt_mineral_modifier` (correctly treats gh_min_d=0 as 'no minimum') and `critical_gh_deficit` (still applies the ratio check via the .max(0.01) guard). While unlikely in practice (requires gh_min_d=0 AND Ca=0 AND Mg=0), it violates the contract that setting gh_min_d=0 disables all GH-related molt penalties."},{"body":"In `update_molt_stress` (shrimp.rs lines 498-504), the `thermal_stress` component only tracks temperatures above `optimal_temp_max_c`. Cold temperatures (below `optimal_temp_min_c`) contribute zero thermal_stress to `molt_stress_index`, even though they reduce molt success via `thermal_factor` in `molt_cycle`. This means chronic cold exposure does not build up molt stress over time — it only causes individual molt failures when they resolve, which then indirectly raise stress via `failed_molt_accum`. Consider adding a symmetric cold-temperature branch: `if temp < optimal_temp_min_c { ((optimal_temp_min_c - temp) / temp_condition_low_divisor_c).clamp(0.0, molt_stress_thermal_cap) }` to match the heat stress path.","rationale":"The asymmetry means that a tank at 10°C has zero molt_stress_index from temperature (only from failed molt accumulation), while a tank at 32°C builds thermal_stress directly into molt_stress_index every tick. Both should build stress gradually. The `temperature_penalty_detail` diagnostic function already handles both cold and hot symmetrically (lines 1710-1719), so the stress tracking should match."}]},"fast_mode_state":"off","uuid":"c1022f0b-8b5b-4992-bc25-447801425b7c"}
